+                 * pad. A client that finds its controller by walking the HID
+                 * interface and reading those ids therefore sees TWO of them,
+                 * and the second answers nothing a controller would.
+                 *
+                 * Sony's own library does exactly that: HidD_GetHidGuid,
+                 * SetupAPI, HidD_GetAttributes. No title using it starts while
+                 * XInputRumble is on, and that has been known and shipped as a
+                 * limitation twice.
+                 *
+                 * It costs nothing to fix because nothing else ever wanted this
+                 * device. xinput does not look for it under the HID interface
+                 * -- dlls/xinput1_3/main.c enumerates GUID_DEVINTERFACE_WINEXINPUT,
+                 * which is registered just above and is untouched here. Every
+                 * other client was only ever going to be confused by it. */
+                if (is_motors_only_collection( desc ))
